t{d}x=5$ and ${\\int }_{3}^{6}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{3}$ then what is ${\\int }_{0}^{6}(3f(x)+3)\\,\\text{d}x?$" :question/worked-solution "From the adjacent intervals rule, we know that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{3}^{6}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x={\\int }_{0}^{6}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nPlugging in the known information into the above gives the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5+\\frac{1}{3}={\\int }_{0}^{6}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\frac{16}{3}={\\int }_{0}^{6}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we compute the desired integral and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{6}(3f(x)+3)\\,\\text{d}x & =3{\\int }_{0}^{6}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x+3{\\int }_{0}^{6}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3(\\frac{16}{3})+3\\cdot x\\,{|}_{0}^{6} \\\\  & =16+3(6-0) \\\\  & =34.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-73350/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9693b76e-ba77-5314-bfbf-508b25bb1072"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-73350"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-346186/field-1/23a7b929cccc5bdeb88db3bdc770afbaf59570d63e930fc5c94f26cb6f5091dc" :answer/id #uuid "e1866726-5e6e-5d37-ae66-77a5dd027662" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "60" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-346186/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "06568dec-b3e7-55d9-9f5b-4bc42d6c1c9b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-346186/field-1/23a7b929cccc5bdeb88db3bdc770afbaf59570d63e930fc5c94f26cb6f5091dc" :answer-field/choices ["q-346186/field-1/23a7b929cccc5bdeb88db3bdc770afbaf59570d63e930fc5c94f26cb6f5091dc"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-346186" :question/id #uuid "a02e085b-165a-538f-ae55-e825e6b5f89f" :question/math-academy-id "q-346186" :question/problem "Given that ${\\int }_{2}^{7}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=3$ and ${\\int }_{7}^{11}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=-10,$ \nthen what is ${\\int }_{2}^{11}(2-6f(x))\\,\\text{d}x?$\n\n${\\int }_{2}^{11}(2-6f(x))\\,\\text{d}x=$ \n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "From the adjacent intervals rule, we know that\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{2}^{7}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x\\,+\\,{\\int }_{7}^{11}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x\\,=\\,{\\int }_{2}^{11}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nPlugging in the known information gives\n\n$$\n3+(-10)\\,=\\,{\\int }_{2}^{11}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x\\,⇒\\,{\\int }_{2}^{11}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=-7.\n$$\n\nFinally, compute the desired integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{2}^{11}(2-6f(x))\\,\\text{d}x & =2{\\int }_{2}^{11}1\\,\\text{d}x\\,-\\,6{\\int }_{2}^{11}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\cdot x{|}_{2}^{11}\\,-\\,6(-7) \\\\  & =2(11-2)+42 \\\\  & =18+42 \\\\  & =60\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-346186/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9693b76e-ba77-5314-bfbf-508b25bb1072"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-346186"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-114138/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "40cebf71-b610-58c4-bb42-4fb90ef0f8a6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-114138/selection/f853eeffac47c628af4a2b7e7b0ecd024652f548b0b0007bc18dba21ad82ad7c" :answer/id #uuid "f61c1445-0106-59a7-b683-c9035bab95a7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-114138/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "69ea1e3d-dc06-55ac-96cb-198a85cb5968" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-114138/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "9e86906b-6482-5407-b3fb-54277787c5e1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-114138/selection/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" :answer/id #uuid "09d10639-77fe-5cb0-9ab7-f266159f785e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-114138/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "9bdfebfc-1c3e-5a02-9e91-b37099a84576" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-114138/selection/f853eeffac47c628af4a2b7e7b0ecd024652f548b0b0007bc18dba21ad82ad7c" :answer-field/choices ["q-114138/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" "q-114138/selection/f853eeffac47c628af4a2b7e7b0ecd024652f548b0b0007bc18dba21ad82ad7c" "q-114138/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" "q-114138/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" "q-114138/selection/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-114138" :question/id #uuid "61ddbb4e-de49-5742-b133-eb07be0fd7de" :question/math-academy-id "q-114138" :question/problem "Given that ${\\int }_{-1}^{1}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=2$ and ${\\int }_{1}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=1,$ then what is ${\\int }_{-1}^{3}(2f(x)-3)\\,\\text{d}x?$" :question/worked-solution "From the adjacent intervals rule, we know that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1}^{1}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{1}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x={\\int }_{-1}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nPlugging in the known information into the above gives the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2+1 & ={\\int }_{-1}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ 3 & ={\\int }_{-1}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we compute the desired integral and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1}^{3}(2f(x)-3)\\,\\text{d}x & =2{\\int }_{-1}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x-3{\\int }_{-1}^{3}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\cdot 3-3\\cdot x\\,{|}_{-1}^{3} \\\\  & =2\\cdot 3-3(3-(-1)) \\\\  & =6-3(4) \\\\  & =-6.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-114138/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9693b76e-ba77-5314-bfbf-508b25bb1072"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-114138"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-346187/field-1/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" :answer/id #uuid "01080b51-c0d9-5a7d-9e36-5bc67d4b4cae" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-346187/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "55dc33ab-63c5-507f-9f01-dd46c490a9e8" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-346187/field-1/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" :answer-field/choices ["q-346187/field-1/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-346187" :question/id #uuid "abacc09f-e24f-5083-9902-ea5b1af36c84" :question/math-academy-id "q-346187" :question/problem "Given that ${\\int }_{4}^{6}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=-1$ and ${\\int }_{6}^{10}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=11,$ \nthen what is ${\\int }_{4}^{10}(6-3f(x))\\,\\text{d}x?$\n\n${\\int }_{4}^{10}(6-3f(x))\\,\\text{d}x=$ \n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "From the adjacent intervals rule, we know that\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{4}^{6}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{6}^{10}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x={\\int }_{4}^{10}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nPlugging in the known information gives\n\n$$\n(-1)+11={\\int }_{4}^{10}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x\\,⇒\\,{\\int }_{4}^{10}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=10.\n$$\n\nFinally, compute the desired integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{4}^{10}(6-3f(x))\\,\\text{d}x & =6{\\int }_{4}^{10}1\\,\\text{d}x-3{\\int }_{4}^{10}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =6\\cdot x{|}_{4}^{10}-3(10) \\\\  & =6(10-4)-30 \\\\  & =36-30 \\\\  & =6\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-346187/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9693b76e-ba77-5314-bfbf-508b25bb1072"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-346187"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-4789/selection/66dedd51c696580d351ab6a45c1c63cb495081ccf219c3c3c62f1d90fbeb5a49" :answer/id #uuid "e0df4282-89c7-5050-b0b3-ff7615b118f2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "15" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-4789/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "81a5eb46-1077-557a-8954-1b42e0011210" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-4789/selection/ae9425c9e204310ed598f729a242e0b42a2acbbf125bff30bc2080e10b8cf473" :answer/id #uuid "e37a82c1-e8f4-56a4-87a1-0f2f6a47f9b0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-4789/selection/83c2285763389b0bc8b13e9777da06a48782d28e9c124603d3003cc4dc2e718a" :answer/id #uuid "33463087-38f5-577d-89f7-5f2eced21970" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "14" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-4789/selection/4e0d8402ce61a9969d16a551582a4c98e6792e5edb3c1272d991dba7d5c92279" :answer/id #uuid "c927b5b8-66d3-52db-8bf0-b3a531fcdb88" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-14" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-4789/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "9ac64c44-89a2-555d-a305-fdb2250b1233" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-4789/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer-field/choices ["q-4789/selection/66dedd51c696580d351ab6a45c1c63cb495081ccf219c3c3c62f1d90fbeb5a49" "q-4789/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" "q-4789/selection/ae9425c9e204310ed598f729a242e0b42a2acbbf125bff30bc2080e10b8cf473" "q-4789/selection/83c2285763389b0bc8b13e9777da06a48782d28e9c124603d3003cc4dc2e718a" "q-4789/selection/4e0d8402ce61a9969d16a551582a4c98e6792e5edb3c1272d991dba7d5c92279"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-4789" :question/id #uuid "ae339ff6-1422-5622-973f-bdc1e90b872b" :question/math-academy-id "q-4789" :question/problem "Suppose that $f(x)$ is a  function such that ${\\int }_{2}^{6}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=9$ and ${\\int }_{9}^{6}4\\,f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=20.$ What is the value of ${\\int }_{2}^{9}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x?$" :question/worked-solution "Let's simplify one of the given integrals:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{9}^{6}4\\,f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =20 \\\\ 4{\\int }_{9}^{6}\\,f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =20 \\\\ -4{\\int }_{6}^{9}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =20 \\\\ {\\int }_{6}^{9}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =-5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, from the adjacent intervals rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{2}^{9}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{2}^{6}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{6}^{9}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =9+(-5) \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-4789/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1d752aac-6187-595d-8818-b0179fd7380e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-4789"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-4795/selection/83c2285763389b0bc8b13e9777da06a48782d28e9c124603d3003cc4dc2e718a" :answer/id #uuid "b5d95299-ac10-5eb9-b5f6-19067958467c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "14" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-4795/selection/0f0db3a18f1d79c4863315eefe754cc5306e04e7aeebf4414ffedb95d6f1bc97" :answer/id #uuid "49e8904f-7cbe-5fcf-8a34-e9861f46e3f3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "12" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-4795/selection/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" :answer/id #uuid "5a48057a-c503-527e-b209-24eb83285ac3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-4795/selection/56019ff80d11d678dbd5eca83c729f420f1b6a8ad4259032846618d6b48aa0bc" :answer/id #uuid "b1a1b409-1a13-52dc-93b6-19a7061f9933" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "10" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-4795/selection/7f2aea1619f9c4cbe5384e0826442d82ebdb1ac614452244ced54b63c0c77efe" :answer/id #uuid "a9ee562e-1a00-517d-81a4-7041ea4d844f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "7" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-4795/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "81ae0418-fa3d-59f6-8cd8-b0a00150d751" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-4795/selection/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" :answer-field/choices ["q-4795/selection/83c2285763389b0bc8b13e9777da06a48782d28e9c124603d3003cc4dc2e718a" "q-4795/selection/0f0db3a18f1d79c4863315eefe754cc5306e04e7aeebf4414ffedb95d6f1bc97" "q-4795/selection/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" "q-4795/selection/56019ff80d11d678dbd5eca83c729f420f1b6a8ad4259032846618d6b48aa0bc" "q-4795/selection/7f2aea1619f9c4cbe5384e0826442d82ebdb1ac614452244ced54b63c0c77efe"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-4795" :question/id #uuid "2f7e1e9b-4799-51a0-a138-eeebd44e608b" :question/math-academy-id "q-4795" :question/problem "Suppose that $f(x)$ is a  function such that ${\\int }_{2}^{7}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=8$ and ${\\int }_{2}^{0}2f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=4.$ What is the value of ${\\int }_{0}^{7}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x?$" :question/worked-solution "Let's simplify one of the given integrals:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{2}^{0}2f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =4 \\\\ 2{\\int }_{2}^{0}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =4 \\\\ -2{\\int }_{0}^{2}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =4 \\\\ {\\int }_{0}^{2}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, from the adjacent intervals rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{7}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{2}^{7}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =(-2)+8 \\\\  & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-4795/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1d752aac-6187-595d-8818-b0179fd7380e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-4795"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-4726/selection/12b7d840a997b0af25896f37c76d366155c72a970c1525c62ec119b69786f393" :answer/id #uuid "ad292ea9-dd5f-5514-b897-9d26801459df" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "13" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-4726/selection/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" :answer/id #uuid "ee03515b-63c9-5a57-a099-0a91174bb038" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-4726/selection/7845f5bf94d2cfe99f73682a34529955af46f8f5d6f59bb198a07cbc245060af" :answer/id #uuid "5dd4e0dc-2414-5dbd-a02c-4ed071f332f4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-4726/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "7c3b158d-7679-5c83-ba2f-9c82989ff367" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-4726/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "e9c8eb6d-129d-5988-aaeb-86043df1b923" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-4726/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "55d599d0-48dd-5bd4-bca8-58ce8dd874e0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-4726/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer-field/choices ["q-4726/selection/12b7d840a997b0af25896f37c76d366155c72a970c1525c62ec119b69786f393" "q-4726/selection/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" "q-4726/selection/7845f5bf94d2cfe99f73682a34529955af46f8f5d6f59bb198a07cbc245060af" "q-4726/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" "q-4726/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-4726" :question/id #uuid "e39e611c-2e6a-5118-851f-9558e33dfe9e" :question/math-academy-id "q-4726" :question/problem "Let $f$ and $g$ be continuous functions such that ${\\int }_{0}^{7}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=18,{\\int }_{0}^{7}\\frac{1}{2}g(x)\\,\\text{d}x=5,$ and ${\\int }_{3}^{7}(f(x)-g(x))\\text{d}x=4.$ What is the value of ${\\int }_{0}^{3}(f(x)-g(x))\\text{d}x?$" :question/worked-solution "Let's simplify one of the given integrals:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{7}\\frac{1}{2}\\,g(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =5 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{7}g(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =5 \\\\ {\\int }_{0}^{7}g(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, using the adjacent intervals rule and substituting the known values, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{7}(f(x)-g(x))\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}(f(x)-g(x))\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{3}^{7}(f(x)-g(x))\\text{d}x \\\\ {\\int }_{0}^{7}(f(x)-g(x))\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}(f(x)-g(x))\\text{d}x+4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, by applying the sum rule for definite integrals and substituting the known values, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{7}(f(x)-g(x))\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}(f(x)-g(x))\\text{d}x+4 \\\\ {\\int }_{0}^{7}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x-{\\int }_{0}^{7}g(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}(f(x)-g(x))\\text{d}x+4 \\\\ 18-10 & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}(f(x)-g(x))\\text{d}x+4 \\\\ 4 & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}(f(x)-g(x))\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, ${\\int }_{0}^{3}(f(x)-g(x))\\text{d}x=4.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-4726/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1d752aac-6187-595d-8818-b0179fd7380e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-4726"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-114153/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "7f9560cb-8f32-5005-957c-e2a5397f366a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-114153/selection/7845f5bf94d2cfe99f73682a34529955af46f8f5d6f59bb198a07cbc245060af" :answer/id #uuid "fe5c6322-a33e-5a7f-8039-937d469dbdf3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-114153/selection/f509030681214332b5989836fe0af4b2eb5858d193e689fd8441dff5cd45ff45" :answer/id #uuid "8237aab3-9a6d-55c8-be4f-a24490c93905" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-12" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-114153/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "12aa52ba-29e3-50a3-9543-de6a3834c635" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-114153/selection/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" :answer/id #uuid "04326036-7645-5b05-84da-8e78cc586097" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-114153/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "7eee6eee-0177-5cb2-b1df-c5fa9e98ace8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-114153/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer-field/choices ["q-114153/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" "q-114153/selection/7845f5bf94d2cfe99f73682a34529955af46f8f5d6f59bb198a07cbc245060af" "q-114153/selection/f509030681214332b5989836fe0af4b2eb5858d193e689fd8441dff5cd45ff45" "q-114153/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" "q-114153/selection/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-114153" :question/id #uuid "79362d8f-ee8e-5edf-a603-e0c270628ab9" :question/math-academy-id "q-114153" :question/problem "Suppose that $f(x)$ is a function such that ${\\int }_{4}^{1}\\frac{1}{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=2$ and ${\\int }_{-1}^{1}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=6.$ What is the value of ${\\int }_{-1}^{4}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x?$" :question/worked-solution "Let's simplify one of the given integrals:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{4}^{1}\\frac{1}{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =2 \\\\ \\frac{1}{3}{\\int }_{4}^{1}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =2 \\\\ -\\frac{1}{3}{\\int }_{1}^{4}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =2 \\\\ {\\int }_{1}^{4}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =-6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, from the adjacent intervals rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1}^{4}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{1}^{4}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =6+(-6) \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-114153/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1d752aac-6187-595d-8818-b0179fd7380e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-114153"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
